flowchart TB
  accTitle: Verified execution of one graph node
  accDescr: The executor selects a topologically ready node, checks its preconditions against the current state, invokes the bound skill, and evaluates its postcondition verifier. A successful check marks the node verified and enables eligible descendants. A failed precondition, execution, postcondition, or timeout creates a typed failure event for local repair.
  R[Ready node selected] --> P[Precondition verification]
  P -->|Pass| E[Execute bound skill]
  P -->|Fail| F[Typed failure event]
  E --> V[Postcondition verifier]
  V -->|Pass| S[Mark node verified]
  V -->|Fail| F
  E -->|Timeout or exception| F
  S --> N[Enable eligible descendants]
  F --> L[Local repair controller]
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class R source
  class P,E,V,L process
  class S,N output
  class F caution
